# black_line — this repository's own ignores.
#
# Black Line is its own repository, so it must carry the ignore rules its own
# documentation asserts. README.md, AGENTS.md, docs/README.md, and
# docs/development.md all state that `output/` is git-ignored and disposable;
# without this file that statement is only true for a checkout that happens to
# sit inside some larger tree whose ignores it inherits. In a separated copy a
# contributor could commit generated artifacts against the project's own stated
# invariant. `tests/test_standalone_contract.py` binds these entries to that
# claim with a real `git check-ignore` run.

# Environments and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.benchmarks/

# Build products of the package itself
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Coverage artifacts
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage_project.json
htmlcov/

# The generated mirror: figures, rendered manuscript, reports. Disposable and
# regenerable from source; never a review artifact in its own right.
output/
